  "body": "## Accepted result and published preprint\n\n**A flow reduction for equilibrium uniqueness in rank-one bimatrix games**, Alec Kriebel. Published paper and verification package: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23430642 (https://zenodo.org/records/23430642).\n\nFor explicitly listed rational bimatrix games of variable positive dimensions and exact rank(A+B)=1, uniqueness of the entire mixed-strategy equilibrium pair is coNP-complete and NONUNIQUENESS is NP-complete, allowing arbitrary degeneracy. A polynomial reduction from nonempty positive-integer PARTITION produces a known strict pure equilibrium and an additional pair exactly in yes instances. The proof applies the Disser\u2013Skutella signed flow counter and the Adsul/coauthors auxiliary zero-sum representation, with a tailored comparison-preserving perturbation, injective simplex encoding and uniform all-minimizer exact penalty. The support package preserves authored original and fresh review evidence. A bounded primary-source audit found no exact match among inspected bodies; worldwide priority remains unknown.\n\n## Accepted scope and review\n\nExactly-one mixed Nash equilibrium pair is coNP-complete for variable-dimension explicit rational rank(A+B)=1 games with degeneracy allowed; known strict default plus second equilibrium iff PARTITION yes.\n\nNo gap asserted under these quantifiers; nondegenerate-promise, strong hardness, fixed dimensions and payoff-uniqueness variants excluded.\n\nThe result is accepted at the exact audited head `ad138ddd5bd1a51c0f225f03342c0c058873f790`. 3 fresh independent complete AI whole-package reviews were completed, with the final review finding zero actionable issues. Subsequent bounded administrative adoption is recorded in the current external ROOT final seal; earlier status/counter/hold fields remain dated history. Prior mathematical results and proof dependencies are credited. Historical novelty and worldwide current openness are unestablished. AI tools were used extensively; this is an unrefereed preprint, without conventional human peer review or formal proof certification.\n\nThe repository Zenodo uploader verified the exact reviewed metadata and PDF/support bytes. The Google Workspace CLI recorded the DOI/details in the requested tracker with exact read-back. No GitHub release is created. Current audit and publication receipts: `audits/pr1041_30003934`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Preserved original PR description: dated submission history</summary>\n\n## Accepted theorem and exact scope\n\nUNIQUENESS of the mixed-strategy equilibrium pair in explicitly encoded rational, variable-dimension bimatrix games with rank(A+B)=1 is coNP-complete. Arbitrary degeneracy is allowed. The reduction from PARTITION to NONUNIQUENESS has a known strict pure default equilibrium and another equilibrium exactly for yes instances. The independent certificate argument supplies the coNP-membership proof, including positive-dimensional equilibrium sets.\n\nThis addresses problem 30003934 / OWR-16413-005, priority rank 1171, on the first substantive approach. No hardness claim under a nondegeneracy promise is made. The proof also does not assert strong hardness, fixed-dimension hardness, or the distinct problem of equilibrium-payoff uniqueness.\n\n## Complete proof and chronological review\n\nThe complete 13,596-byte proof, complete 15,545-byte certificate report, full 18,916-byte conditional mathematical audit, and subsequent 3,042-byte hash-specific final acceptance are included byte-for-byte. The early audit records the all-optimal-flow source-quantifier gap and all corrections. The later acceptance confirms that the unchanged final manuscript incorporates them and has no unresolved mathematical blocker. The edition acceptance explains the historical candidate header without editing the accepted proof.\n\nA separate complete reading accepted the same scoped theorem. Acceptance rests on the written perturbation, residual-cycle uniqueness, injective simplex embedding, uniform all-minimizer exact penalty, rank-one equilibrium correspondence, strict default pair, full parameter coverage and polynomial binary encoding, together with the rational-certificate argument. Historical finite-check discussion remains in the full proof and audit, but no executable, fixture, separate result or log is distributed.\n\n## Attribution and limits\n\nThe [rank-one parameter-family correspondence](https://doi.org/10.1287/opre.2020.1981) and [Disser\u2013Skutella parametric-flow construction](https://doi.org/10.1145/3280847) are established prior work. The present written proof supplies the required all-optimal-flow strengthening and rank-preserving bridge; it does not infer that strengthening from the source corollary alone. The strict-default pattern is also known in unrestricted bimatrix-game hardness. Full attribution and bounded related-work review are included. No novelty, historical priority, or exhaustive current-open-status claim is made.\n\nThese are AI mathematical/source audits, not external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant verification.\n\n## Exact addition-only boundary\n\nAdd exactly eleven files under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003934/`. No QUEUE.md or unrelated file is changed. No copied third-party source documents, source text or images, datasets, derived source-text fingerprints, private sources, private storage paths or coordination files are included. Public PDF identities and inspection history are metadata only. Hashes and clean additive-patch replay check packaging integrity, not mathematical truth. Draft for review; no merge or release is requested.\n\n## Exact file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.md`: 4,304 bytes; SHA-256 `9d858ae4eaabfcf697ce9166df71a566a2b0b49d1f0b38b457b5c1cf9096fa5d`\n- `ATTRIBUTION.md`: 13,373 bytes; SHA-256 `757cc706e40642d67373f5d81e553cf794bdcb98959baca852c3593126d4908f`\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 2,273 bytes; SHA-256 `9415e942d10a43b535be8fa71138612c15963dfb40b7bb40560b95a862cd0a19`\n- `PROOF.md`: 13,596 bytes; SHA-256 `5392acc347fe0eaf8597ac619341b2946d21781e6118676248a4ee83baad6c1b`\n- `PROVENANCE.md`: 4,242 bytes; SHA-256 `03c22f37ce26b6950d873220b6d50a2f6377531229d556e009fc490ee631ead6`\n- `README.md`: 3,108 bytes; SHA-256 `44b3cb32efda9feea56c8e7914a71f1cfda0703f0ac1eecdaba0cf0f099c9f27`\n- `SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json`: 12,385 bytes; SHA-256 `f5a635ec0211b78fe63a54da8e9f43400ec18f8386713e1ecbcdd0c4f8cf6762`\n- `STATUS.json`: 2,483 bytes; SHA-256 `032dd89b67a5c07750a7fab8626c0ae7cff6f372d184323719eae2b928a79b99`\n- `certificates/LEMMA_REPORT.md`: 15,545 bytes; SHA-256 `c498514fa147cce010ad5a4bd90eefd9dd2532d70edbf5930e85520ae65862e6`\n- `independent_audit/AUDIT.md`: 18,916 bytes; SHA-256 `c0d1ae53175d4ae02815930b3ca305f430aaf0a6dc893b1d8a23bf18a979847f`\n- `independent_audit/FINAL_ACCEPTANCE.md`: 3,042 bytes; SHA-256 `a994e2b0f0b2bb3dac88aa0bab907351ce8b18cd6a45786843ea7569195ef324`\n\nThe manifest lists all eleven members and hashes the other ten; this body pins the manifest independently.\n\n\n</details>\n",
